"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[54813],{54813:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n\\n<center>\\n<RestaurantCard\\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/location/a4646e76e8c1af5982452c6a900db4d9.jpg\\"\\n          title=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\"\\n          cuisine=\\"Buckwheat Noodles\\"\\n          address=\\"7-7 Yanggok 2-ro 30beon-gil, Yangchon-eup, Gimpo-si, Gyeonggi-do\\"\\n          rating=4.5\\n          tags=\\"restaurant\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nAfter wrapping up our Chuseok holiday schedule, we decided to spend the whole day lounging around and resting.  \\nStill, we needed to have lunch, so we looked for a good place to eat out.  \\nWhile searching around, we found a makguksu (buckwheat noodles) spot we\'d like that had great reviews and an appealing menu, so we headed there without hesitation.  \\nThey had a dedicated parking lot for the restaurant, so driving there was completely hassle-free.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nIt\'s usually packed enough to require waiting—even having a <mark>CatchTable</mark> system—but perhaps because of the holiday, we were lucky enough to walk right in without waiting.  \\nEven so, the inside of the restaurant was completely full of diners.  \\n\\nAfter debating what to order, we chose our favorite, <mark>Perilla Seed Makguksu</mark>, and the barley rice set.  \\nIn reality, rather than a set menu, it felt more like barley rice was served as a complimentary starter, similar to how barley rice often comes with kalguksu (knife-cut noodles).  \\nThe barley rice was served right after ordering, accompanied by locally sourced vegetables, seasoned greens (namul), and what tasted like homemade gang-doenjang (thick seasoned soybean paste) to mix in as you like.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nA great perk was the self-service bar, where you could bring more greens and gang-doenjang to enjoy a hearty bowl.  \\nWe love bracken (gosari), so we brought extra bracken and lettuce to our table.  \\nThe gang-doenjang alone was seasoned well enough to enjoy a mild, savory taste, and it was nice that gochujang (red pepper paste) was also provided separately so you could add it to your liking.  \\nIn particular, we added some sesame oil that tasted like it was freshly pressed at a traditional mill; the sesame oil was so delicious that it made us feel the barley rice alone would have been completely satisfying.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nAs we were eating the barley rice, our makguksu arrived shortly after.  \\nThe perilla seed makguksu was nutty and savory, with slightly less sweetness than the typical version we knew.  \\nIt was delicious as it was, but since we usually prefer a generous amount of perilla oil, we added plenty of extra perilla oil.  \\nOn top of that, we added bracken in our own style, and the refreshing, nutty flavor was truly fantastic.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nIt was a hearty and delicious meal combining great makguksu and barley rice.  \\nNormally, we would always order the large portion for makguksu, but with the barley rice included, the regular size was plenty.  \\n\\nLooking at the restaurant wall, there was a notice saying they are expanding and relocating, and we look forward to even more people being able to enjoy this great taste.  \\nWe were left wishing it were closer to our home so we could visit much more often.\\n## Pictures\\n<pictures>\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/a4646e76e8c1af5982452c6a900db4d9.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/285b4b2e04cb70727192bcfd7032cb7e.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/c7925ee15481c14da6ccffea86647075.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/1d8ea1c0eadf08754ebb2c4668e25e33.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/9ca049e5239ff3581dc1867a55ee80aa.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/5fbe6a4b6289950b305139b2e3a284cb.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/3cfef4199c52bd280762f89cbf7a5d89.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/55ec4012ef4faeca8e647cf5321e3795.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n<img src=\\"/assets/snippets/location/037a3a6493a289dc60bd50e628dc4017.jpg\\" style=\\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; object-fit: contain;\\" alt=\\"Baekyang Makguksu Yanggok Branch\\">\\n</pictures>"}')}}]);